                  <provenance type="#e m"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_474">St Albans,
                        Hertfordshire. Benedictine abbey of St Alban</orgName><p>'Hic scribuntur
                        nomina fratrum de professione sancti Albani defunctorum a susceptione
                        fratris Iohannis de Walingef' in eodem ordine uidelicet a die sanctorum
                        Dionisii Eustici 7 Eleutherii anno ab incarnatione domini mo cco xxxo primo'
                        (fol. 112v).</p><p>Contains writing in the hand of Matthew Paris (see R.
                        Vaughan, 'The handwriting of Matthew Paris', Transactions of the Cambridge
                        Bib. Soc. 1 (1953) 390--92).</p><p>Portrait on fol. 42v headed 'Frater
                        Iohannes de Walingeford quandoque Infirmarius'.</p><p>'Hic(?) est liber
                        frater Iohannis de Walingeford quem [ . . . ] uel [ . . . ] uel inde [ . . .
                        . . . ] sit amen amen' (fol. 1v in red).</p><p>'Constat Iohanni Conyngesby
                        ex dono Magistri Kyngesbury' (fol. 1r, s. xv).</p><p>See Wormald, English
                        Benedictine Kalendars after 1100, p. 32.</p><p>Fols. 50--53 are now bound
                        separately.</p></provenance>
               </history>
